with the variation which had occurred in Fairhurst-Michell in round 6, where
there is an opportunity for both players to have two queens on the board but
again the option was rejected. Saunders later lost or gave up the exchange for
a pawn (isolated on the d-file). Tylor won the extra pawn and gained a victory
before adjournment time. (Source: BCM, Sep 1932, p380)} 1-0

